<title>USA: Wages, productivity not fueling prices - White House.</title>
<headline>Wages, productivity not fueling prices - White House.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Top White House economic adviser Joseph Stiglitz said Thursday that growing U.S. wages and productivity were not pressuring inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;One of the good things about productivity increasing is that you can get increases in real wages without inflationary pressures,&quot; Stiglitz said at a news briefing.</p>
<p>Stiglitz, who is chairman of the White House Council of Economic Advisers, said that wages were increasing faster than inflation, but not so fast that they would lead to the kinds of interest rate increases that would dampen economic growth.</p>
</text>
